# Definition of Done

A change is complete when all **applicable** items below are satisfied.

## Code and architecture

- [ ] Respects feature-module layers (`10-architecture.mdc`)
- [ ] Imports use feature barrels from tests for state/services only (presentation via fixtures)
- [ ] TypeScript strict mode — no unjustified `any`
- [ ] `npm run typecheck` passes
- [ ] `npm run lint` passes
- [ ] `npm run build` passes (`pw-core` compiles)

## Tests

- [ ] New behavior covered by appropriate layer (api / integration / e2e / hybrid / functional)
- [ ] `specs/test.plan.md` updated if scenarios changed
- [ ] Existing tests updated when locators or flows change
- [ ] Hybrid tests use `page.request` when session cookies matter

## Documentation

- [ ] README updated if user-facing behavior changed
- [ ] ADR added for architectural decisions (see `30-documentation.mdc`)
- [ ] `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` updated if structure or diagrams changed

## Verification

- [ ] UI/API behavior verified against the demo store when observable (IronBee or Playwright)
- [ ] No secrets committed; credentials only via `.env` / CI secrets

## CI alignment

- [ ] Changes compatible with `.github/workflows/quality-gates.yml`
- [ ] Wishlist E2E: credential policy per ADR-002 (local skip; GitHub skips without secrets; Docker fails when `@wishlist` runs)
